# A latch on registers whose header φs read each other: the search for
# the reason its trip count is not read visits each register once and
# ends, where it recursed until the stack overflowed (13 census kernels);
# the loop's trip count is unknown, and why is named.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/swap_latch.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB0_1: // loop: trips ? (uniform(%r2@$L__BB0_1) is defined in an enclosing loop: depends on %r2, carried around an enclosing loop) | warp * × lane * | exec ?{{$}}
